# Jerk Rice and Peas Bowl

Based on [https://www.africanbites.com/one-pot-caribbean-jerk-chicken-rice/](https://www.africanbites.com/one-pot-caribbean-jerk-chicken-rice) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251211144227/https://www.africanbites.com/one-pot-caribbean-jerk-chicken-rice/)) and [https://www.thekitchn.com/jerk-chicken-jamaican-rice-and-peas-recipe-256069](https://www.thekitchn.com/jerk-chicken-jamaican-rice-and-peas-recipe-256069) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251003064825/https://www.thekitchn.com/jerk-chicken-jamaican-rice-and-peas-recipe-256069))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Jerk Seasoning

- [ ] 2 tsp [allspice]{ ing="allspice" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried thyme]{ ing="dried-thyme" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [onion powder]{ ing="onion-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" } (adjust for heat preference)
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [nutmeg]{ ing="nutmeg" }

### Rice and Peas

- [ ] 1.5 cups [long-grain brown rice]{ ing="long-grain-brown-rice" } (or brown/white rice blend)
- [ ] 1 (15 oz) can [red kidney beans]{ ing="red-kidney-beans" }, drained and rinsed
- [ ] 1 (14 oz) can [coconut milk]{ ing="coconut-milk" } (full-fat)
- [ ] 1 cup [water or chicken broth]{ ing="water-or-chicken-broth" }
- [ ] 3 [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, chopped (white and green parts separated)
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 2 sprigs fresh [thyme]{ ing="thyme" } (or 1 tsp dried thyme)
- [ ] 1 [scotch bonnet]{ ing="scotch-bonnet" } or habanero pepper, whole (optional, for heat)

### Protein Options (choose one)

- [ ] 1.5 lbs [boneless chicken thighs]{ ing="boneless-chicken-thighs" }, cut into 1-inch pieces
- [ ] 1.5 lbs [extra-firm tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, pressed and cubed
- [ ] 1 lb [shrimp]{ ing="shrimp" }, peeled and deveined

### Bowl Toppings

- [ ] 1 [ripe mango]{ ing="ripe-mango" }, diced
- [ ] 1/2 [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" }, thinly sliced and pickled in lime juice
- [ ] 1 [avocado]{ ing="avocado" }, sliced
- [ ] Fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, chopped
- [ ] 2 [limes]{ ing="limes" }, cut into wedges
- [ ] [Scotch bonnet crema]{ ing="scotch-bonnet-crema" } (optional): 1/4 cup sour cream or Greek yogurt mixed with 1 tsp minced scotch bonnet and 1 Tbsp lime juice

## Recipe

### Prepare the Jerk Seasoning and Marinate

1. In a small bowl, combine all jerk seasoning ingredients
1. Reserve 1 Tbsp of jerk seasoning for the [rice]{ ing="long-grain-brown-rice" }
1. In a large bowl, toss the protein with remaining jerk seasoning and 1 Tbsp oil. Let marinate for at least 30 minutes (or up to 24 hours refrigerated)

### Make the Rice and Peas

1. In a large pot or Dutch oven with lid, heat 1 Tbsp oil over medium heat
1. Add white parts of [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" } and [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, cook until fragrant (~1 min)
1. Add brown rice and reserved 1 Tbsp jerk seasoning, toast for 2-3 minutes, stirring frequently
1. Add [coconut milk]{ ing="coconut-milk" }, water/[broth]{ ing="water-or-chicken-broth" }, [kidney beans]{ ing="red-kidney-beans" }, [thyme]{ ing="dried-thyme" } sprigs, and whole [scotch bonnet]{ ing="scotch-bonnet" } [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" } (if using)
1. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer for 40-45 minutes until rice is tender and liquid is absorbed
1. Remove from heat, discard thyme sprigs and scotch bonnet pepper. Stir in green parts of green onions. Keep covered

### Cook the Protein

1. For chicken: Heat 1 Tbsp oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Cook chicken pieces 5-7 minutes per side until cooked through (internal temp 165F) and slightly charred. Alternatively, air fry at 400F for 12-15 minutes, shaking halfway
1. For [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }: Air fry at 400F for 15-18 minutes until crispy, or pan-fry in 2 Tbsp oil over medium-high heat for 3-4 minutes per side
1. For [shrimp]{ ing="shrimp" }: Cook in skillet with 1 Tbsp oil over medium-high heat for 2-3 minutes per side until pink and opaque

### Assemble Bowls

1. Divide rice and peas among serving bowls
1. Top with cooked protein, [mango]{ ing="ripe-mango" }, pickled [red onions]{ ing="red-onion" }, [avocado]{ ing="avocado" }, and [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }
1. Serve with [lime]{ ing="limes" } wedges and [scotch bonnet crema]{ ing="scotch-bonnet-crema" } if desired

## Notes

- **Traditional preparation:** Uses white rice and cooks for 20-25 minutes. Brown rice adds fiber and has lower glycemic impact but takes longer to cook
- **Flavor/texture tradeoff with brown rice:** Brown rice has a nuttier, chewier texture compared to fluffy white rice. The coconut milk helps keep it creamy. If you prefer traditional texture, use a 50/50 white/brown rice blend
- **Spice level:** The whole scotch bonnet adds flavor without much heat (don’t pierce it). Remove it if concerned about spice
- **Meal prep:** Rice and peas reheat well. Store protein separately and reheat gently to avoid drying out
- **Make ahead:** Pickle the red onions up to 1 week in advance. Marinate protein up to 24 hours ahead
